<title>USA: Hanover to make $50 mln rights offering.</title>
<headline>Hanover to make $50 mln rights offering.</headline>
<dateline>WEEHAWKEN, N.J. 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hanover Direct Inc said Wednesday that it would recapitalise through a $50 million rights offering.</p>
<p>The company said the rights would be priced at $0.90 per share of common stock and that Richemont, an affiliate of Hanover's majority shareholder, has agreed to buy all shares not subscribed by Hanover's shareholders.</p>
<p>It said Richemont has agreed to advance it up to $30 million to facilitate improved vendor shipments.</p>
<p>Additionally, Hanover said its lender group has waived compliance with covenants of its $75 million credit facility through December 28 and amended other convenants.</p>
<p>Two Richemont executives Jan du Plessis and Howard Tanner, will be joining the Hanover board, the company said.</p>
</text>
